{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789301180,"nonce":"CdSCy26g8Gme5hHb6yTfWRQGDSM=","title":"Host registration: bind to a class the program already declares","message":"register_host_module refuses a class whose name the program declares.\nThe HL target refuses extern class, so a class a host wants Haxe code to\ntype against is always compiled into the program by the host's build\nmacro, and the host then cannot register under that name. Today the\nhost registers a differently named companion and the program's natives\nbind by (lib, name), which works but leaves the program's class and the\nhost's description as two things.\n\nAdd a mode where registration finds the program's class by name,\nverifies its fields and protos agree with the host's description (same\nnames, same hashes, compatible types), and attaches the host's natives\nto the (lib, name) pairs the class declares, refusing on disagreement\nwith a diagnostic naming both. Related: hot reload re-decodes from disk\nand loses registrations (apply_pending_reload), and\nType.resolveClass(\"host.X\") cannot see a host-only class.","files":null}]}